Artifact checklist
==================

Scope
-----
Supports the static-audit and behavioral-confirmation claims in Sections 4-5
of the paper: corpus construction, canonical-vs-modal divergence, popularity
stratification, upstream-drift timestamps, hand-validation of the refusal
classifier, and the ModelScope external-validity check. Does not cover the
Ollama registry entries (tracked separately, not part of the primary result).

Hardware
--------
No GPU required. Static audit is API calls + local parsing, runs fine on a
laptop. Behavioral pilots need a machine that can run 7-9B GGUF models via
Ollama at reasonable speed -- CPU-only is fine but slow (a pilot run took
several hours on consumer-grade CPU-only hardware).

Software
--------
Python 3.10+, packages in requirements.txt (requests, jinja2). Ollama
installed locally with mistral:7b, phi3:3.8b, gemma2:9b, qwen2.5:7b,
llama3.1:8b pulled for the behavioral pilots. No other services needed --
everything else talks directly to the public HF and ModelScope APIs.

Data
----
data/raw/ has the corpus build logs and exclusion lists. data/results/ has
every static-audit output plus the ModelScope corpus. experiments/*/ has the
per-anchor behavioral pilot transcripts and jinja templates actually tested.
All of it is included in this repo already -- nothing needs to be downloaded
separately except the model weights themselves via Ollama.

Estimated time
--------------
Static audit against the existing corpus_v2.json: under an hour, mostly API
rate-limit waiting. Full corpus rebuild from scratch: a few hours, HF's
search API is the bottleneck. Behavioral pilots: budget half a day per
anchor if re-running from scratch on CPU-only hardware.

